Z||000000||LPR||03-21-2001||07:13 PM||||This place is great! I have another problem with my 84 though, it has a real erratic idle.  I don’t know what’s wrong with it.  When I start the car it revs at 2000 until warmed up and then goes down to 1000, but sometimes it will fall below 1000 and back up again and then fall again until it stalls.  Also, when I hit the gas pedal or take it out of gear while driving it will race and stay there for a long time before returning to 1000.  <P>Luc<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||03-21-2001||09:42 PM||||Hey Luc!<BR>First start with the vacuume lines...<BR>Replace them all if you want the best results, as the hard plastic cracks and leaks too...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||862M4inCA||03-21-2001||09:52 PM||||hrm. you might check the MAP sensor. My grandma had an old grand marquis (88) and it had a real erratic idle, but instead of revving up, it would surge (rev up, try to return to idle, go below and almost die, repeat). We tried everything including rechecking all vacuum connections, resealing the intakeand numerous other items, and finally got to the MAP sensor, replaced it, and problems disappeared. BTW, have you noticed any engine codes stored in the ECM?||||reg||1
Z||000003||LPR||03-21-2001||10:04 PM||||Complicated answer to that one! I have replaced a engine that had the same problem before it died!  The car has a new computer and engine, I'm pretty sure the vacume lines came with the "new" engine.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Smokin87||03-21-2001||10:41 PM||||Hey, <BR>have you checked the o2 sensors?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||btoth||03-22-2001||10:04 PM||||My GT has always fluctuated like 862M4inCA said... before and after the rebuild of the engine.  It will usally idle right at 900RPM (when warmed up) but at completely random times (usually when in park) the idle will fall to about 500RPM and sound like it wants to stall and kicks up to about 1300RPM and repeats this over and over.  I have replaced all vacuum lines (except the egr valve line - which looks fine) with the steel lines and all sensors have been replaced with the engine rebuild (some more than once).  Anyone have any ideas what would cause this random occurance?<P>PS - What brand sensors to you use?  Should I stick with ACDelco if possible?  Because I doubt that most of them are at this point.||||reg||1
